    Value: 420 KM
  - Label: ONE ORBIT
    Value: 1.12 DAYS
  - Label: DISTANCE FROM NEPTUNE
    Value: 117,647 KM
  - Label: SURFACE GRAVITY
    Value: 0.007 G
  - Label: DISCOVERED
    Value: 1989, VOYAGER 2
  description: Neptune's second-largest moon is one of the darkest objects in the solar system, reflecting only about a tenth of the light that reaches it. It is about as large as a moon can be without pulling itself round.
